#, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalence of the representations"
msgstr "Equivalencia de las representaciones"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore vectorizing */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore bilinearity */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore vectorizing */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore bilinearity */}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've now discussed three different ways to represent channels in mathematical terms, namely Stinespring representations, Kraus representations, and Choi representations.\n"
"We also have the definition of a channel, which states that a channel is a linear mapping that always transforms density matrices into density matrices, even when the channel is applied to just part of a compound system.\n"
"The remainder of the lesson is devoted to a mathematical proof that the three representations are equivalent and precisely capture the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ya hemos visto tres formas distintas de representar canales en términos matemáticos: las representaciones de Stinespring, las representaciones de Kraus y las representaciones de Choi.\n"
"También tenemos la definición de canal, que establece que un canal es una aplicación lineal que siempre transforma matrices de densidad en matrices de densidad, incluso cuando el canal se aplica solo a una parte de un sistema compuesto.\n"
"El resto de la lección está dedicado a la demostración matemática de que las tres representaciones son equivalentes y capturan con precisión la definición.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview of the proof {#overview-of-the-proof}"
msgstr "Panorama general de la demostración {#overview-of-the-proof}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our goal is to establish the equivalence of a collection of four statements, and we'll begin by writing them down precisely.\n"
"All four statements follow the same conventions that have been used throughout the lesson, namely that $\\Phi$ is a linear mapping from square matrices to square matrices, the rows and columns of the input matrices have been placed in correspondence with the classical states of a system $\\mathsf{X}$ (the input system), and the rows and columns of the output matrices have been placed in correspondence with the classical states of a system $\\mathsf{Y}$ (the output system).\n"
msgstr ""
"Nuestro objetivo es establecer la equivalencia de un conjunto de cuatro enunciados, y comenzaremos escribiéndolos con precisión.\n"
"Los cuatro enunciados siguen las mismas convenciones que se han usado a lo largo de la lección: $\\Phi$ es una aplicación lineal de matrices cuadradas a matrices cuadradas, las filas y columnas de las matrices de entrada se han puesto en correspondencia con los estados clásicos de un sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ (el sistema de entrada), y las filas y columnas de las matrices de salida se han puesto en correspondencia con los estados clásicos de un sistema $\\mathsf{Y}$ (el sistema de salida).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Phi$ is a channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$. That is, $\\Phi$ always transforms density matrices to density matrices, even when it acts on one part of a larger compound system.\n"
msgstr "$\\Phi$ es un canal de $\\mathsf{X}$ a $\\mathsf{Y}.$ Es decir, $\\Phi$ siempre transforma matrices de densidad en matrices de densidad, incluso cuando actúa sobre una parte de un sistema compuesto mayor.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Choi matrix $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite and satisfies the condition $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr "La matriz de Choi $J(\\Phi)$ es semidefinida positiva y satisface la condición $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a Kraus representation for $\\Phi$. That is, there exist matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ for which the equation $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}$ is true for every input $\\rho$, and that satisfy the condition $\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr "Existe una representación de Kraus para $\\Phi$. Es decir, existen matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ para las cuales la ecuación $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}$ es verdadera para toda entrada $\\rho$, y que satisfacen la condición $\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a Stinespring representation for $\\Phi$. That is, there exist systems $\\mathsf{W}$ and $\\mathsf{G}$ for which the pairs $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ and $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ have the same number of classical states, along with a unitary matrix $U$ representing a unitary operation from $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ to $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, such that $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}}\\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger} \\bigr)$.\n"
msgstr "Existe una representación de Stinespring para $\\Phi$. Es decir, existen sistemas $\\mathsf{W}$ y $\\mathsf{G}$ para los cuales los pares $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ y $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ tienen el mismo número de estados clásicos, junto con una matriz unitaria $U$ que representa una operación unitaria de $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ a $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, tal que $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}}\\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger} \\bigr)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way the proof works is that a cycle of implications is proved:\n"
"the first statement in our list implies the second, the second implies the third, the third implies the fourth, and the fourth statement implies the first.\n"
"This establishes that all four statements are equivalent — which is to say that they're either all true or all false for a given choice of $\\Phi$ — because the implications can be followed transitively from any one statement to any other.\n"
msgstr ""
"La forma en que funciona la demostración es probando un ciclo de implicaciones:\n"
"el primer enunciado de nuestra lista implica el segundo, el segundo implica el tercero, el tercero implica el cuarto, y el cuarto enunciado implica el primero.\n"
"Esto establece que los cuatro enunciados son equivalentes —es decir, que son todos verdaderos o todos falsos para una elección dada de $\\Phi$— porque las implicaciones se pueden seguir de forma transitiva desde cualquier enunciado hasta cualquier otro.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a common strategy when proving that a collection of statements are equivalent, and a useful trick to use in such a context is to set up the implications in a way that makes them as easy to prove as possible.\n"
"That is the case here — and in fact we've already encountered two of the four implications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta es una estrategia habitual cuando se demuestra que un conjunto de enunciados son equivalentes, y un truco útil en este contexto es organizar las implicaciones de manera que sean lo más fáciles de demostrar posible.\n"
"Ese es el caso aquí —y de hecho ya hemos visto dos de las cuatro implicaciones.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Channels to Choi matrices {#channels-to-choi-matrices}"
msgstr "De canales a matrices de Choi {#channels-to-choi-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Referring to the statements listed above by their numbers, the first implication to be proved is 1 $\\Rightarrow$ 2.\n"
"This implication was already discussed in the context of the Choi state of a channel.\n"
"Here we'll summarize the mathematical details.\n"
msgstr ""
"Refiriéndonos a los enunciados listados anteriormente por sus números, la primera implicación a demostrar es 1 $\\Rightarrow$ 2.\n"
"Esta implicación ya se discutió en el contexto del estado de Choi de un canal.\n"
"Aquí resumiremos los detalles matemáticos.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assume that the classical state set of the input system $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\Sigma$ and let $n = \\vert\\Sigma\\vert$.\n"
"Consider the situation in which $\\Phi$ is applied to the second of two copies of $\\mathsf{X}$ together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos que el conjunto de estados clásicos del sistema de entrada $\\mathsf{X}$ es $\\Sigma$ y sea $n = \\vert\\Sigma\\vert$.\n"
"Consideremos la situación en la que $\\Phi$ se aplica al segundo de dos copias de $\\mathsf{X}$ juntas en el estado\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\sum_{a \\in \\Sigma} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\sum_{a \\in \\Sigma} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which, as a density matrix, is given by\n"
msgstr "que, como matriz de densidad, viene dado por\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b \\in \\Sigma}\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b \\in \\Sigma}\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result can be written as\n"
msgstr "El resultado se puede escribir como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\operatorname{Id}\\otimes \\,\\Phi) \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\Phi\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{J(\\Phi)}{n},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\operatorname{Id}\\otimes \\,\\Phi) \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\Phi\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{J(\\Phi)}{n},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and by the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel this must be a density matrix.\n"
"Like all density matrices it must be positive semidefinite, and multiplying a positive semidefinite matrix by a positive real number yields another positive semidefinite matrix, and therefore $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"y por la suposición de que $\\Phi$ es un canal, esto debe ser una matriz de densidad.\n"
"Como toda matriz de densidad, debe ser semidefinida positiva, y multiplicar una matriz semidefinida positiva por un número real positivo da otra matriz semidefinida positiva, por lo tanto $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moreover, under the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel, it must preserve trace, and therefore\n"
msgstr "Además, bajo la suposición de que $\\Phi$ es un canal, debe preservar la traza, y por lo tanto\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\Phi( \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert)\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\Phi( \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert)\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choi to Kraus representations {#choi-to-kraus-representations}"
msgstr "De la representación de Choi a la de Kraus {#choi-to-kraus-representations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second implication, again referring to the statements in our list by their numbers, is 2 $\\Rightarrow$ 3.\n"
"To be clear, we're ignoring the other statements — and in particular we cannot make the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel.\n"
"All we have to work with is that $\\Phi$ is a linear mapping whose Choi representation satisfies $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$ and\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"La segunda implicación, refiriéndonos de nuevo a los enunciados de nuestra lista por sus números, es 2 $\\Rightarrow$ 3.\n"
"Para ser claros, estamos ignorando los demás enunciados — y en particular no podemos asumir que $\\Phi$ sea un canal.\n"
"Todo lo que tenemos para trabajar es que $\\Phi$ es una aplicación lineal cuya representación de Choi satisface $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$ y\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This, however, is all we need to conclude that $\\Phi$ has a Kraus representation\n"
msgstr "Esto, sin embargo, es todo lo que necesitamos para concluir que $\\Phi$ tiene una representación de Kraus\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for which the condition\n"
msgstr "para la cual la condición\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is satisfied.\n"
msgstr "is satisfied.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We begin with the critically important assumption that $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite, which means that it is possible to express it in the form\n"
msgstr "Comenzamos con la suposición de importancia crítica de que $J(\\Phi)$ es semidefinida positiva, lo que significa que es posible expresarla en la forma\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for some way of choosing the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$.\n"
"In general there will be multiple ways to do this — and in fact this directly mirrors the freedom one has in choosing a Kraus representation for $\\Phi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"para alguna elección de los vectores $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$.\n"
"En general habrá múltiples formas de hacer esto —y de hecho esto refleja directamente la libertad que se tiene al elegir una representación de Kraus para $\\Phi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One way to obtain such an expression is to first use the spectral theorem to write\n"
msgstr "Una manera de obtener dicha expresión es usar primero el teorema espectral para escribir\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\gamma_k \\rangle \\langle \\gamma_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\gamma_k \\rangle \\langle \\gamma_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "in which $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$ are the eigenvalues of $J(\\Phi)$ (which are necessarily nonnegative real numbers because $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite) and $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{N-1}\\rangle$ are unit eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalues $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$.\n"
msgstr "donde $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$ son los valores propios de $J(\\Phi)$ (que son necesariamente números reales no negativos porque $J(\\Phi)$ es semidefinida positiva) y $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{N-1}\\rangle$ son vectores propios unitarios correspondientes a los valores propios $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that, while there's no freedom in choosing the eigenvalues (except for how they're ordered), there is freedom in the choice of the eigenvectors, particularly when there are eigenvalues with multiplicity larger than one.\n"
"So, this is not a unique expression of $J(\\Phi)$ — we're just assuming we have one such expression.\n"
"Regardless, because the eigenvalues are nonnegative real numbers, they have nonnegative square roots, and so we can select\n"
msgstr ""
"Observa que, aunque no hay libertad al elegir los valores propios (excepto en cómo se ordenan), sí hay libertad en la elección de los vectores propios, especialmente cuando hay valores propios con multiplicidad mayor que uno.\n"
"Por lo tanto, esta no es una expresión única de $J(\\Phi)$ —simplemente asumimos que tenemos una de esas expresiones.\n"
"De todas formas, como los valores propios son números reales no negativos, tienen raíces cuadradas no negativas, por lo que podemos seleccionar\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\gamma_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\gamma_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for each $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$ to obtain an expression of the form $(1)$.\n"
msgstr "para cada $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$ y obtener una expresión de la forma $(1)$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, however, not essential that the expression $(1)$ comes from a spectral decomposition in this way, and in particular the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ need not be orthogonal in general.\n"
"It is noteworthy, though, that we can choose these vectors to be orthogonal if we wish — and moreover we never need $N$ to be larger than $nm$\n"
"(recalling that $n$ and $m$ denote the numbers of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$, respectively).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, no es esencial que la expresión $(1)$ provenga de una descomposición espectral de esta manera, y en particular los vectores $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ no tienen por qué ser ortogonales en general.\n"
"Vale la pena señalar, no obstante, que podemos elegir estos vectores de forma que sean ortogonales si así lo deseamos —y además nunca necesitamos que $N$ sea mayor que $nm$\n"
"(recordando que $n$ y $m$ denotan los números de estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$, respectivamente).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, each of the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ can be further decomposed as\n"
msgstr "A continuación, cada uno de los vectores $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ se puede descomponer adicionalmente como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the vectors $\\{ \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle \\}$ have entries corresponding to the classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ and can be explicitly determined by the equation\n"
msgstr "donde los vectores $\\{ \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle \\}$ tienen entradas correspondientes a los estados clásicos de $\\mathsf{Y}$ y pueden determinarse explícitamente mediante la ecuación\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle = \\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigr) \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle = \\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigr) \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for each $a\\in\\Sigma$ and $k=0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"
"Although $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ are not necessarily unit vectors, this is the same process we would use to analyze what would happen if a standard basis measurement was performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$ given a quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"para cada $a\\in\\Sigma$ y $k=0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"
"Aunque $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ no son necesariamente vectores unitarios, este es el mismo proceso que usaríamos para analizar qué ocurriría si se realizara una medición en la base estándar sobre el sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ dado un vector de estado cuántico del par $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now we come to the trick that makes this part of the proof work.\n"
"We define our Kraus matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ according to the following equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Y ahora llegamos al truco que hace funcionar esta parte de la demostración.\n"
"Definimos nuestras matrices de Kraus $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ según la siguiente ecuación.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can think about this formula purely symbolically: $\\vert a\\rangle$ effectively gets flipped around to form $\\langle a\\vert$ and moved to right-hand side, forming a matrix.\n"
"For the purposes of verifying the proof, the formula is all we need.\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos pensar en esta fórmula de forma puramente simbólica: $\\vert a\\rangle$ se \"gira\" para formar $\\langle a\\vert$ y se mueve al lado derecho, formando una matriz.\n"
"Para los propósitos de verificar la demostración, la fórmula es todo lo que necesitamos.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is, however, a simple and intuitive relationship between the vector $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ and the matrix $A_k$, which is that by *vectorizing* $A_k$ we get $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$.\n"
"What it means to vectorize $A_k$ is that we stack the columns on top of one another (with the leftmost column on top proceeding to the rightmost on the bottom), in order to form a vector.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are both qubits, and for some choice of $k$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, hay una relación simple e intuitiva entre el vector $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ y la matriz $A_k$, que es que *vectorizando* $A_k$ obtenemos $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$.\n"
"Lo que significa vectorizar $A_k$ es que apilamos las columnas una sobre otra (con la columna más a la izquierda en la parte superior y la más a la derecha en la parte inferior) para formar un vector.\n"
"Por ejemplo, si $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ son ambos qubits, y para alguna elección de $k$ tenemos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then\n"
msgstr "entonces\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A_k & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{10}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A_k & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{10}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Beware: sometimes the vectorization of a matrix is defined in a slightly different way, which is that the *rows* of the matrix are transposed and stacked on top of one another to form a column vector.)\n"
msgstr "(Atención: a veces la vectorización de una matriz se define de una manera ligeramente diferente, en la que las *filas* de la matriz se transponen y se apilan una sobre otra para formar un vector columna.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First we'll verify that this choice of Kraus matrices correctly describes the mapping $\\Phi$, after which we'll verify the other required condition.\n"
"To keep things straight, let's define a new mapping $\\Psi$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero verificaremos que esta elección de matrices de Kraus describe correctamente la aplicación $\\Phi$, y después verificaremos la otra condición requerida.\n"
"Para no perder el hilo, definamos una nueva aplicación $\\Psi$ de la siguiente manera.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Psi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Psi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, our goal is to verify that $\\Psi = \\Phi$.\n"
msgstr "Así, nuestro objetivo es verificar que $\\Psi = \\Phi$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way we can do this is to compare the Choi representations of these mappings.\n"
"Choi representations are faithful, so we have $\\Psi = \\Phi$ if and only if $J(\\Phi) = J(\\Psi)$.\n"
"At this point we can simply compute $J(\\Psi)$ using the expressions\n"
msgstr ""
"La forma de hacerlo es comparar las representaciones de Choi de estas aplicaciones.\n"
"Las representaciones de Choi son fieles, de modo que $\\Psi = \\Phi$ si y solo si $J(\\Phi) = J(\\Psi)$.\n"
"En este punto podemos simplemente calcular $J(\\Psi)$ usando las expresiones\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{y}\\quad\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "together with the bilinearity of tensor products to simplify.\n"
msgstr "junto con la bilinealidad del producto tensorial para simplificar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Psi) & = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert A_k^{\\dagger}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1}  \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle b\\vert \\otimes \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\\biggr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = J(\\Phi)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Psi) & = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert A_k^{\\dagger}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1}  \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle b\\vert \\otimes \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\\biggr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = J(\\Phi)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So, our Kraus matrices correctly describe $\\Phi$.\n"
msgstr "Por lo tanto, nuestras matrices de Kraus describen correctamente $\\Phi$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to check the required condition on $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$, which turns out to be equivalent to the assumption $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ (which we haven't used yet).\n"
"What we'll show is this relationship:\n"
msgstr ""
"Queda verificar la condición requerida sobre $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$, que resulta ser equivalente a la suposición $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ (que aún no hemos usado).\n"
"Lo que demostraremos es esta relación:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr)^{T} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr)^{T} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(in which we're referring the *matrix transpose* on the left-hand side).\n"
msgstr "(donde nos referimos a la *transpuesta matricial* en el lado izquierdo).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Starting on the left, we can first observe that\n"
msgstr "Comenzando por la izquierda, podemos observar primero que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T\n"
"& = \\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)^T\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T\n"
"& = \\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)^T\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last equality follows from the fact that the transpose is linear and maps $\\vert b\\rangle\\langle a \\vert$ to $\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert$.\n"
msgstr "La última igualdad se sigue del hecho de que la transpuesta es lineal y aplica $\\vert b\\rangle\\langle a \\vert$ a $\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moving to the right-hand side of our equation, we have\n"
msgstr "Pasando al lado derecho de nuestra ecuación, tenemos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k \\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k \\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and therefore\n"
msgstr "y por lo tanto\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\bigr)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\bigr)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've obtained the same result, and therefore the equation $(2)$ has been verified.\n"
"It follows, by the assumption $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, that\n"
msgstr ""
"Hemos obtenido el mismo resultado, por lo que la ecuación $(2)$ ha sido verificada.\n"
"Se sigue entonces, por la suposición $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and therefore, because the identity matrix is its own transpose, the required condition is true.\n"
msgstr "y por lo tanto, dado que la matriz identidad es su propia transpuesta, la condición requerida es verdadera.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Kraus to Stinespring representations {#kraus-to-stinespring-representations}"
msgstr "De representaciones de Kraus a representaciones de Stinespring {#kraus-to-stinespring-representations}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now suppose that we have a Kraus representation of a mapping\n"
msgstr "Supongamos ahora que tenemos una representación de Kraus de un mapeo\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for which\n"
msgstr "para el cual se cumple\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our goal is to find a Stinespring representation for $\\Phi$.\n"
msgstr "Nuestro objetivo es encontrar una representación de Stinespring para $\\Phi$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What we'd like to do first is to choose the garbage system $\\mathsf{G}$ so that its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"For $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ and $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ to have the same size, however, it must be that\n"
"$n$ divides $m N$, allowing us to take $\\mathsf{W}$ to have classical states $\\{0,\\ldots,d-1\\}$ for $d = mN/n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lo que queremos hacer primero es elegir el sistema basura $\\mathsf{G}$ de modo que su conjunto de estados clásicos sea $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"Sin embargo, para que $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ y $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ tengan el mismo tamaño, es necesario que\n"
"$n$ divida a $m N$, lo que nos permite tomar $\\mathsf{W}$ con estados clásicos $\\{0,\\ldots,d-1\\}$ para $d = mN/n$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For an arbitrary choice of $n$, $m$, and $N$, it may not be the case that $mN/n$ is an integer, so we're not actually free to choose $\\mathsf{G}$ so that it's classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"But we can always increase $N$ arbitrarily in the Kraus representation by choosing $A_k = 0$ for however many additional values of $k$ that we wish.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para una elección arbitraria de $n,$ $m$ y $N,$ puede darse que $mN/n$ no sea un entero, así que en realidad no tenemos libertad para elegir $\\mathsf{G}$ de manera que su conjunto de estados clásicos sea $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Pero siempre podemos aumentar $N$ arbitrariamente en la representación de Kraus eligiendo $A_k = 0$ para tantos valores adicionales de $k$ como deseemos.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we tacitly assume that $mN/n$ is an integer, which is equivalent to $N$ being a multiple of $n/\\operatorname{gcd}(n,m)$, then we're free to take $\\mathsf{G}$ so that its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"In particular, if it is the case that $N = nm$, then we may take $\\mathsf{W}$ to have $m^2$ classical states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Entonces, si suponemos tácitamente que $mN/n$ es un entero, lo cual equivale a que $N$ sea múltiplo de $n/\\operatorname{gcd}(n,m)$, podemos elegir $\\mathsf{G}$ de modo que su conjunto de estados clásicos sea $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"En particular, si $N = nm$, entonces podemos tomar $\\mathsf{W}$ con $m^2$ estados clásicos.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It remains to choose $U$, and we'll do this by matching the following pattern.\n"
msgstr "Queda elegir $U$, y lo haremos siguiendo el siguiente patrón.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, this pattern is meant to suggest a block matrix, where each block (including $A_{0},\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ as well as the blocks marked with a question mark) has $m$ rows and $n$ columns.\n"
"There are $N$ rows of blocks, which means that there are $d = mN/n$ columns of blocks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ser preciso, este patrón representa una matriz en bloques, donde cada bloque (incluyendo $A_{0},\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ así como los bloques marcados con signo de interrogación) tiene $m$ filas y $n$ columnas.\n"
"Hay $N$ filas de bloques, lo que implica que hay $d = mN/n$ columnas de bloques.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressed in more formulaic terms, we will define $U$ as\n"
msgstr "Expresado de forma más formulaica, definiremos $U$ como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U & = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\sum_{j=0}^{d-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle j \\vert \\otimes M_{k,j} \\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} & \\cdots & M_{0,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1} & \\cdots & M_{1,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{N-1,0} & M_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & M_{N-1,d-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U & = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\sum_{j=0}^{d-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle j \\vert \\otimes M_{k,j} \\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} & \\cdots & M_{0,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1} & \\cdots & M_{1,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{N-1,0} & M_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & M_{N-1,d-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where each matrix $M_{k,j}$ has $m$ rows and $n$ columns, and in particular we shall take $M_{k,0} = A_k$ for $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"
msgstr "donde cada matriz $M_{k,j}$ tiene $m$ filas y $n$ columnas, y en particular tomaremos $M_{k,0} = A_k$ para $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This must be a unitary matrix, and the blocks labeled with a question mark, or equivalently $M_{k,j}$ for $j>0$, must be selected with this in mind — but aside from allowing $U$ to be unitary, the blocks labeled with a question mark won't have any relevance to the proof.\n"
msgstr "Esta debe ser una matriz unitaria, y los bloques marcados con signo de interrogación, equivalentemente $M_{k,j}$ para $j>0$, deben elegirse con eso en mente — pero más allá de permitir que $U$ sea unitaria, dichos bloques no tendrán ninguna relevancia en la prueba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's momentarily disregard the concern that $U$ is unitary and focus on the expression\n"
msgstr "Dejemos de lado momentáneamente la preocupación de que $U$ sea unitaria y concentrémonos en la expresión\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that describes the output state of $\\mathsf{Y}$ given the input state $\\rho$ of $\\mathsf{X}$ for our Stinespring representation.\n"
"We can alternatively write\n"
msgstr ""
"que describe el estado de salida de $\\mathsf{Y}$ dado el estado de entrada $\\rho$ de $\\mathsf{X}$ para nuestra representación de Stinespring.\n"
"Podemos escribir alternativamente\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) \\rho (\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) U^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) \\rho (\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) U^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and we see from our choice of $U$ that\n"
msgstr "y vemos a partir de nuestra elección de $U$ que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We therefore find that\n"
msgstr "Por lo tanto obtenemos que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert \\otimes A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert \\otimes A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and so\n"
msgstr "and so\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"& = \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert\\bigr) \\, A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\Phi(\\rho).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"& = \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert\\bigr) \\, A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\Phi(\\rho).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We therefore have a correct representation for the mapping $\\Phi$, and it remains to verify that we can choose $U$ to be unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Consideremos las primeras $n$ columnas de $U$ cuando se elige según el patrón anterior.\n"
"Tomando solo esas columnas, obtenemos la matriz en bloques\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the first $n$ columns of $U$ when it's selected according to the pattern above.\n"
"Taking these columns alone, we have a block matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Considera las primeras $n$ columnas de $U$ cuando se selecciona según el patrón anterior.\n"
"Tomando solo estas columnas, tenemos una matriz por bloques\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are $n$ columns, one for each classical state of $\\mathsf{X}$, and as vectors let us name the columns as $\\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Here's a formula for these vectors that can be matched to the block matrix representation above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hay $n$ columnas, una para cada estado clásico de $\\mathsf{X}$, y como vectores nombremos las columnas como $\\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle$ para cada $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Aquí hay una fórmula para estos vectores que puede ser relacionada con la representación de matriz de bloques anterior.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\gamma_a\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\gamma_a\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's compute the inner product between any two of these vectors, meaning the ones corresponding to any choice of $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr "Ahora calculemos el producto interno entre cualesquiera dos de estos vectores, es decir, los correspondientes a cualquier elección de $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle k \\vert j \\rangle \\, \\langle a \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} A_j \\vert b\\rangle =\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr) \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle k \\vert j \\rangle \\, \\langle a \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} A_j \\vert b\\rangle =\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr) \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By the assumption\n"
msgstr "Por la suposición\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "we conclude that the $n$ column vectors $\\{\\vert\\gamma_a\\rangle\\,:\\,a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ form an orthonormal set:\n"
msgstr "concluimos que los $n$ vectores columna $\\{\\vert\\gamma_a\\rangle\\,:\\,a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ forman un conjunto ortonormal:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & a = b\\\\\n"
"0 & a\\neq b\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & a = b\\\\\n"
"0 & a\\neq b\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto implica que es posible completar las columnas restantes de $U$ de modo que se convierta en una matriz unitaria.\n"
"En particular, se puede utilizar el proceso de ortogonalización de Gram-Schmidt para seleccionar las columnas restantes.\n"
"Algo similar se hizo en la lección de *Circuitos cuánticos* de \"Fundamentos de información cuántica\" en el contexto del problema de discriminación de estados.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that it is possible to fill out the remaining columns of $U$ so that it becomes a unitary matrix.\n"
"In particular, the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process can be used to select the remaining columns.\n"
"Something similar was done in the *Quantum circuits* lesson of \"Basics of quantum information\" in the context of the state discrimination problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto implica que es posible completar las columnas restantes de $U$ para que se convierta en una matriz unitaria.\n"
"En particular, se puede usar el proceso de ortogonalización de Gram-Schmidt para seleccionar las columnas restantes.\n"
"Algo similar se hizo en la lección *Circuitos cuánticos* de \"Fundamentos de la información cuántica\" en el contexto del problema de discriminación de estados.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stinespring representations back to the definition {#stinespring-representations-back-to-the-definition}"
msgstr "De representaciones de Stinespring de vuelta a la definición {#stinespring-representations-back-to-the-definition}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The final implication is 4 $\\Rightarrow$ 1.\n"
"That is, we assume that we have a unitary operation transforming a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ into a pair\n"
"$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, and our goal is to conclude that the mapping\n"
msgstr ""
"La implicación final es 4 $\\Rightarrow$ 1.\n"
"Es decir, suponemos que tenemos una operación unitaria que transforma un par de sistemas $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ en un par\n"
"$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$, y nuestro objetivo es concluir que el mapeo\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a valid channel.\n"
"From its form, it is evident that $\\Phi$ is linear, and it remains to verify that it always transforms density matrices into density matrices.\n"
"This is pretty straightforward and we've already discussed the key points.\n"
msgstr ""
"es un canal válido.\n"
"Por su forma, es evidente que $\\Phi$ es lineal, y queda verificar que siempre transforma matrices de densidad en matrices de densidad.\n"
"Esto es bastante directo y ya hemos discutido los puntos clave.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, if we start with a density matrix $\\sigma$ of a compound system $(\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$, and then add on an additional workspace system $\\mathsf{W}$, we will certainly be left with a density matrix.\n"
"If we reorder the systems $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$ for convenience, we can write this state as\n"
msgstr ""
"En particular, si comenzamos con una matriz de densidad $\\sigma$ de un sistema compuesto $(\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$, y luego añadimos un sistema de espacio de trabajo adicional $\\mathsf{W}$, ciertamente obtendremos una matriz de densidad.\n"
"Si reordenamos los sistemas $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$ por conveniencia, podemos escribir este estado como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\sigma.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\sigma.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then apply the unitary operation $U$, and as we already discussed this is a valid channel, and hence maps density matrices to density matrices.\n"
"Finally, the partial trace of a density matrix is another density matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Luego aplicamos la operación unitaria $U$, y como ya discutimos, esta es un canal válido y por lo tanto mapea matrices de densidad en matrices de densidad.\n"
"Finalmente, la traza parcial de una matriz de densidad es otra matriz de densidad.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another way to say this is to observe first that each of these things is a valid channel:\n"
msgstr "Otra forma de expresar esto es observar primero que cada una de las siguientes cosas es un canal válido:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing an initialized workspace system.\n"
msgstr "Introducir un sistema de espacio de trabajo inicializado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performing a unitary operation.\n"
msgstr "Realizar una operación unitaria.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tracing out a system.\n"
msgstr "Trazar un sistema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "And finally, any composition of channels is another channel — which is immediate from the definition, but is also a fact worth observing in its own right.\n"
msgstr "Y finalmente, cualquier composición de canales es otro canal — lo cual se desprende inmediatamente de la definición, pero es también un hecho que vale la pena observar por sí mismo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This completes the proof of the final implication, and therefore we've established the equivalence of the four statements listed at the start of the section.\n"
msgstr "Esto completa la prueba de la implicación final, y con ello hemos establecido la equivalencia de los cuatro enunciados listados al comienzo de la sección.\n"
